{"id": "EUVD-2026-103710", "enisaUuid": "ee48c0f7-2e20-3d54-9dc1-1b9812157429", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: arm64: Don't WARN on an unknown VM ioctl in protected mode\n\nkvm_pkvm_ioctl_allowed() WARNs when kvm_get_cap_for_kvm_ioctl() doesn't\nfind the ioctl number in vm_ioctl_caps[], and kvm_arch_vm_ioctl() calls\nit for every number the generic code doesn't handle, so\nioctl(vm_fd, 0xdeadbeef) from userspace taints a pKVM host and panics it\nunder panic_on_warn. The lookup is fed userspace input: return false,\nand userspace gets the -EINVAL kvm_arch_vm_ioctl() returns for that\nnumber on a host without pKVM.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:15:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:20:08", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cc53eb5c6515e3221314624a22c9da9c80a67f63", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/49d9d295d69d07e850cae35933ba8519e2915f26"], "aliases": ["GHSA-j632-93gc-r86q", "CVE-2026-98470"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0da32f32-63d9-3a4d-af31-200ce1ba3e92", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "2c4ea033-456e-3dbd-8f39-2d96abd06af6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b12b3b04f6ba072ca5a618a75e546c996be94bd1 <49d9d295d69d07e850cae35933ba8519e2915f26"}, {"id": "3846edff-e065-3c65-b45e-f5fbcabe8b26", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b12b3b04f6ba072ca5a618a75e546c996be94bd1 <cc53eb5c6515e3221314624a22c9da9c80a67f63"}, {"id": "6f4709d7-a305-37b0-adae-b1cdebf23883", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.0"}, {"id": "a9e316d9-f5db-3f3f-a44c-19bbd02ebd2b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "f655cf86-4735-3403-8635-7cb660751ea3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "